 States suffer and this  is not in a situation that any American  president can ultimately tolerate  something has to be done about that  nuclear program shouldn't tolerate but  President Trump said that he would be  honored to meet with him and called him  a smart cookie the well he is a smart  cookie  he would have survived that long so  let's let's let's be clear that he  obviously knows what he's doing  look at the president United States  can't meet with Kim jong-un and  certainly not under these circumstances  there may come a day if North Korea  gives up its nuclear weapons program and  so forth and so on that having North  Korea back in the community of states or  in the community of states would be  worthwhile are you really not there the  armies that will never happen unless we  get the chinese involved in a bigger way  that's right the chinese we've got to  change their calculation right now they  seem more worried about the potential  collapse of the regime and doing hard  things to the regime that about a  nuclear North Korea I think that's what  the administration is trying to do is to  change that calculus so that the Chinese  see that if they don't deal with the  North Koreans we will among others have  said that the terms of the Trump  government has in his national security  a group of very smart people yes what  worries you about the trunk up but this  is an outstanding team all of them and  that is very comforting this is a  president who's never been in the  government I think it's taking them some  time to understand first of all that  it's really hard in there it's not as  easy as it was that it was it is hard  and and secondly yes the president's  words matter and I think that you're  starting to see that reaction he is  reacting to the presidency for instance  in Syria when an American president sees  Syrian babies choking on chemical gas an  American president says I cannot let  that stand no matter what they said when  they were a candidate when their  president they say something different  and do something different and I think  we're starting to see that evolution I  certainly hope so you know Sally Yates  is testifying today before the Senate  Judiciary Committee what are the key  questions that need to be asked of her  today well obviously we're all waiting  to hear what she's going to say and far  be it for me to be the person to ask the  questions but we do need to understand  what was going on before the  inauguration of the President look there  can only be one president at a time and  it is not unusual to meet with foreign  dignitaries ambassadors when you're in  transition that's not unusual at all I  did myself is the National Security  Advisor elect thanks for president  george w bush  you can't you can't discuss policy and  you can't suggest that you might change  policy and so we'll see what really  happened here thank you so much pleasure  to Eddie Lee

